  "tier": "sol",
  "complexity": 5,
  "title": "Q1: orchestrator/planner_taxonomy.py \u2014 decision taxonomy for Planner invocations (purpose over complexity), pure and testable (P2)",
  "spec": "Why: decision.py routes points by kind (held/scouts_done/closable) and risk, but nothing names the PURPOSE of a Planner decision; the router (Q4), telemetry (Q2) and Planner scorecard (Q5) need a stable decision_type to group by (brief .orchestrator/planner-routing-program.md P2).\nWhat: new pure module orchestrator/planner_taxonomy.py; no bus reads, no config reads, inputs never mutated.\n- DECISION_TYPES = (\"initial_goal_plan\", \"scout_results\", \"held_task\", \"architectural_replan\", \"fix_strategy\", \"closable_goal\", \"retrospective\", \"ambiguous_requirement\", \"other\").\n- classify(point, ctx, *, goal=None, task=None) -> {\"decision_type\", \"architectural\": bool, \"ambiguous\": bool, \"risk_class\": \"none\"|\"low\"|\"high\", \"signals\": [str], \"band\", \"task_class\"}. point is planner_runs' dict {goal_id, kind, payload_key, task_id?}; ctx is decision.route's ctx (see orchestrator/decision.py docstring and planner_runs.build_ctx lines 1002-1062); goal/task are bus task dicts or None.\n- Rules, first match wins: kind \"retrospective\" -> retrospective. kind \"scouts_done\": ctx.scout_count == 0 -> initial_goal_plan, else scout_results. kind \"held\": ctx.signature_repeated or ctx.spec_review_request_changes >= 2 or ctx.auto_fix_rounds_used >= ctx.auto_fix_rounds -> architectural_replan; else ctx.failing_ids non-empty or ctx.in_scope_review_comments -> fix_strategy; else held_task. kind \"closable\" -> closable_goal. Unknown kind -> other. After that, ambiguous_requirement overrides initial_goal_plan/scout_results when the goal text (title + spec) carries ambiguity markers: two or more of the tokens \"or\", \"either\", \"unclear\", \"tbd\", \"?\", \"conflict\", \"maybe\", \"alternatively\" (case-insensitive, whole words, \"?\" counted per occurrence), or ctx.get(\"ambiguous\") is True; signals records which markers fired.\n- architectural = attribution.task_class(task or goal) in (\"architectural\", \"security\") or (complexity >= 7) or ctx.touches_interfaces or ctx.touches_migrations or decision_type == architectural_replan; use task complexity for held, goal complexity otherwise.\n- risk_class: high when ctx.touches_auth or ctx.touches_data_deletion or ctx.security_trigger or task_class == \"security\"; low when ctx.touches_interfaces or ctx.touches_migrations or ctx.semantic_trigger; else none. Missing ctx fields count as False/0 and add signal \"unknown:<field>\" (never raise).\n- band via attribution.band(complexity); task_class via attribution.task_class(task or goal) guarded so a missing pool.toml never raises (attribution already guards).\n- explain(classification) -> one line string \"type=... arch=... risk=... signals=a,b\".\nDocstring states purpose-over-complexity with the example: a complexity 8 closable_goal is routine, a complexity 6 ambiguous_requirement is not.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_planner_taxonomy.py::test_held_with_failing_tests_is_fix_strategy \u2014 held ctx with failing_ids and no risk flags classifies fix_strategy, architectural False, risk none",
    "tests/test_planner_taxonomy.py::test_repeated_signature_is_architectural_replan \u2014 held ctx with signature_repeated True classifies architectural_replan and architectural True regardless of complexity 3",
    "tests/test_planner_taxonomy.py::test_scouts_done_without_scouts_is_initial_goal_plan \u2014 scout_count 0 gives initial_goal_plan; scout_count 2 gives scout_results",
    "tests/test_planner_taxonomy.py::test_ambiguity_markers_override_to_ambiguous_requirement \u2014 goal spec 'use redis or postgres, unclear which?' classifies ambiguous_requirement with signals naming the markers; a plain spec does not",
    "tests/test_planner_taxonomy.py::test_risk_and_missing_fields_never_raise \u2014 touches_auth True gives risk high; a ctx missing every optional field classifies without raising and lists unknown:<field> signals; closable kind gives closable_goal at complexity 8 with architectural True"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/planner_taxonomy.py",
    "tests/test_planner_taxonomy.py"
  ],
